# SERTAO

**System for Estimation of Cosmological paRameTers and Analysis of Observables**

<p align="center">
  <img src="docs/logo.png" width="400">
</p>

---

## Implemented Likelihoods and Data Sets

The following likelihoods and data sets are currently implemented:

- BAO – DESI (DR2)
- Angular BAO (2D)
- Type Ia Supernovae – Pantheon+
- Pantheon+ calibrated with SH0ES
- Type Ia Supernovae – Union 3.0
- Primordial Nucleosynthesis prior (BBN)
- Compressed CMB likelihood
- Redshift-Space Distortions (RSD)
- Cosmic Chronometers (CC)

---

## Code Structure and Philosophy

The execution flow of the code has been designed to be simple, modular, and transparent for the user.  
Any cosmological model can be straightforwardly implemented within the SERTAO framework and tested against the data sets listed above (see the manual below).

The `HybridCosmology` module implements a hybrid cosmological framework that combines the internal SERTAO infrastructure with the Boltzmann solver CLASS. This approach provides a flexible background description while benefiting from the precision and robustness of CLASS for perturbation-level calculations.

